From e8aa4afb38069416ce2eb4f02ef79e9e378e4d84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:22:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-90: five XAML Designer keyboard shortcuts
 (Ctrl+Shift+A, F9, Alt+arrows, Ctrl+N, Shift ratio) (0.90.0)

From the XAML Designer keyboard shortcuts page and Blend's resize page:
- Ctrl+Shift+A "Clear all selections": the probe selects nothing (the
  multi-selection too).
- F9 "Show/hide element handles": the selection box, its tag, the handles,
  the other selected boxes and the guides are hidden until F9 again; clicks
  still select; the status says so.
- Alt+arrow "Duplicate an element": ht9045Designer.duplicate (dx, dy) = the
  Ctrl+drag copy of the selection, moved 1 px that way (Shift+Alt = 10 px).
- Ctrl+N "Create an element": the toolbox quick pick (addComponent).
  Both are bound only while the design surface itself has the focus
  (!sideBarFocus && !panelFocus && !auxiliaryBarFocus && !inQuickOpen):
  Alt+Left elsewhere stays VS Code's Go Back, Ctrl+N a new file.
- Shift on a corner handle keeps the proportions (the change of the side that
  changed most, both sides by that factor).

WPF_DIFF_LOG.md: items 15-19 done (0.89 commit filled in); 20 (F2 edits the
control text) is next.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 159, smoke 181, panels, real VS Code 156):
probe (Ctrl+Shift+A -> select null; F9: 8 handles -> 0 (the box too) -> 8;
Shift corner drag 30,2 -> 242x46 to 272x52); smoke (Shift+Alt+Right copy 10 px
right, the 8 keys and Ctrl+N and their when); real VS Code (the duplicate drawn
in Panel2, one undo).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
